{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Sally Comes Home", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Finally in My Own Bed", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 14, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le14ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Past Tense and Past Continuous Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events that are finished. You use the Past Continuous to talk about events or an action that was happening at a time in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "I talked to my mum about my adventures while she was making coffee.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I was counting sheep until 3 a.m. when I finally closed my eyes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Simple Past tense verbs can be regular or irregular.</p> Regular verbs end in <span class=\"strong\">-ed</span> or <span class=\"strong\">-ied</span>.</p> For Past Continuous, we add <span class=\"strong\">was/were</span> + verb\u201c<span class=\"strong\">ing</span>\u201d to verbs.</p> You use Past Continuous verbs to describe a longer action that is interrupted by a shorter action.</p> You use Simple Past verbs to describe the shorter action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were having\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"eat\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ate\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were eating\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"visit\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"visited\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were visiting\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"feel\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"felt\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were feeling\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"catch\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"caught\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were catching\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"hurt\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"hurt\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were hurting\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Making and Responding to Requests", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "It's important to be polite when you ask for something or respond to requests.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can make a request by using: <ul><li>Can you ... ?</li> <li>Could you ... ?</li> <li>Will you ... ?</li> <li>Would you mind ... ?</li>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Making Request</span>: <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>Could you tell me if there is some medication I could take?</li> <li>Could you please be careful with my suitcase?</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Responding to request</span>: <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>Sure, here you are.</li> <li>Yes, I'd love to!</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "jet lag", "type": "name"}, {"content": "physical effects you feel after a long trip across several time zones", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I don't deal with jet lag very well.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le14ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words to review.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "handler", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who takes luggage from a plane to the baggage carousel", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Boston Airport luggage handlers are the best in the country!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le14ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "memento", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that is kept as a reminder of a person, place, or thing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'll take Pugsly back to my apartment as a little momento.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le14ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "comforter", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a thick bed covering that is filled with a soft light material ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You even kept my old unicorn comforter with the rainbows.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le14ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to count sheep", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to close your eyes and count to help you fall asleep", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was counting sheep until 2 a.m. last night when I finally fell asleep!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le14ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "inflamed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "red and swollen, often because of an infection", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My throat is inflamed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le14ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "airsick", "type": "name"}, {"content": "suffering from motion sickness in an aircraft", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I felt airsick on the flight to Boston.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le14ob11aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sleep-deprived", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the feeling of not getting enough sleep", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This jet lag is terrible! I am so sleep-deprived!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le14ob11aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a blog (10-12 lines) about the last holiday you took.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Where was it? How long were you away?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Did you have an accident or were you ill?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Were you happy to come home? What did you miss about home?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your blog aloud to your partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write about my last holiday.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about a health problem.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I say what I was doing when something happened.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can make and respond to requests. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about common health problems. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk or report about actions, events or people.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"c